#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166589 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "4dac81da-f15c-55ff-9630-7349a3e03e57" :question/math-academy-id "e-8273" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](images/9e/9eca81c24ee88a63d1c5468160a118cb1e987793d5fdc8d2d7eaa317fadeda93.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](images/8c/8c3fce8e9d7cc170ad66706e783c4a46ba0530c119b8b824a66d9b5850e62760.svg)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166590 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "aac4b559-b26b-57b0-8701-b3235969cd2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8274" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n![](images/b9/b9a1cb7eb2a3bcbadd73a68f9e73914e124a2359b8f8fc1ccc33ca950e714f88.svg)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](images/9b/9b978860f45e9e62e0315727c8eafac13360f29a7762480103b087ed6babf376.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/88/88ea80808ca87358b78cf322c8ddd81ad7f95ddc02526361aace1ca9b914d486.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](images/c5/c57b6f1ce1762add9b5b5d3e15a6363f009482b12b12366434c090d6a7478c6b.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166591 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "f0fc412f-8276-5876-a509-4f2173396e72" :question/math-academy-id "e-8275" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/27/271f2b051a53f7aeae9a20ef23b97c9c903a7815f228dfa3ee23e2207bd24ee9.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](images/1f/1fc60fff97ff92bd1cc515e6c984fbacb435dcf0fae24e751842eb8daf3390e8.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60dfab55-c3a7-5053-a806-fcfe8f588c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242051} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5294c8-d8c9-5297-918a-01f823aa20fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242137} {:answer/id #uuid "89ba7e99-4fce-561d-a4f7-97c8a8d3a693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242392} {:answer/id #uuid "b077affe-907f-589d-b858-1f4bb4db1ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242718} {:answer/id #uuid "db8c2ebf-94a1-5efe-9d93-7cfdd2ccc046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89ba7e99-4fce-561d-a4f7-97c8a8d3a693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242392} :answer-field/id #uuid "beaa72ad-0454-5661-afee-7e98536209ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86779615-b7e9-524a-8c43-851c650510ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-106731" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482825} {:answer/id #uuid "452b28d8-b289-5fff-a092-488eae620713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482932} {:answer/id #uuid "4d32b03a-dd94-5a69-92a8-4e06c57efc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482949} {:answer/id #uuid "d30f044d-eab8-573d-9ea1-d54b5212aef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483167} {:answer/id #uuid "f0944f13-4475-5463-ad63-c07789ef499b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482825} :answer-field/id #uuid "3657d7a8-9e63-5bda-b364-5472d3ebc7e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6139fff-4bc1-54e3-9731-cfafa322d577" :question/math-academy-id "q-106737" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15301301-2403-50d4-a624-ab391b2dc478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241363} {:answer/id #uuid "376486a2-8e17-5715-a7ad-737fa78c1258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241667} {:answer/id #uuid "48d12868-f91f-5e4d-be31-2ca61761e838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241840} {:answer/id #uuid "7d679e70-9da7-5202-a81d-707bd1efa619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242278} {:answer/id #uuid "8468e60b-9874-537b-9d9b-53bca61026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15301301-2403-50d4-a624-ab391b2dc478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241363} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd008c33-82db-5fa0-8507-c0d8e860acf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33e006b4-f466-5a45-99fb-a4284803e97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106738" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-1)\\cdot (1+t+{t}^{2})+1\\cdot (1+t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-t-{t}^{2}+1+t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171d0343-234f-5fe6-ae55-3ece477e9207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241379} {:answer/id #uuid "1aff8046-3006-51dc-9d3b-ba6796a7edff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241413} {:answer/id #uuid "383e7692-3d26-54f4-b948-270e340894fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241680} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc0df0f-565a-5abe-bc7f-0ad73e9c9925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242551} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ba3108-94ed-5ce5-a92d-da1866021645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171d0343-234f-5fe6-ae55-3ece477e9207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241379} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be8ead8-847d-5795-a57c-1f6ade3aed08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26318539-0a92-5f1e-bd5d-2a9d71f1f3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-106754" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=20 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=14 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+2=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1554fed7-affd-52c8-9b9d-11f75d6528f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482850} {:answer/id #uuid "82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483040} {:answer/id #uuid "b08ae541-af63-5e99-b15c-65086e6b98be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483112} {:answer/id #uuid "eda9481b-28f6-5a31-b610-2b56f853aa8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483212} {:answer/id #uuid "f6906166-88a4-5fdd-88ad-88c8265bc930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483040} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead372e1-7a0e-5867-a1cd-4c08293d91a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04ab001d-eb12-502f-a292-54d2ac24e44a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106761" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-18 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -18 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -18 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+(-3) & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+(-3)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a0b30ef-23c9-5a40-b2b7-3a08fd314751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364718} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a6567-a3c5-5daf-807a-9e1a4a447383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364719} {:answer/id #uuid "a99f142a-ddd6-50dc-9caa-fa0de50f607a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364720} {:answer/id #uuid "503f41ba-227d-5f03-85de-359503fb3f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364721} {:answer/id #uuid "91adae6f-2d17-5175-afff-8df6226b9b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d70a6567-a3c5-5daf-807a-9e1a4a447383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364719} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e961fb-5cce-5fcc-9474-06f333c566e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b159d2dd-0e2d-5b06-aef5-5b4b243d4d01" :question/math-academy-id "q-106777" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -12 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 6{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2\\cdot (-2) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-2)=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128ce6e3-dc22-5943-ae78-9ca654be08a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482842} {:answer/id #uuid "48750a06-11eb-5111-88f7-360fb2f33835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482941} {:answer/id #uuid "5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482969} {:answer/id #uuid "87819992-b54e-5a67-ad9b-1e74d374d74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483048} {:answer/id #uuid "b0025512-e99f-5297-ba08-5bbf9b2b1291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482969} :answer-field/id #uuid "d571972e-d66f-51ff-ad55-ae539c035701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4795a7a-dbd7-5cec-b948-e685d7225538" :question/math-academy-id "q-106778" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ {x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second,  third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2\\cdot 2+3=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2c8aab-876d-5beb-969f-37e4397cc77b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482830} {:answer/id #uuid "7afabdb1-8cf6-5bb2-8ddb-f74a538d8214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483026} {:answer/id #uuid "91c5c0e4-5b53-5efc-880e-e4be1aa2d6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483068} {:answer/id #uuid "b70925f5-b4ec-58fa-86b0-e31569e83883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483122} {:answer/id #uuid "f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483224} :answer-field/id #uuid "77937620-6a66-58b9-a30b-f689a9264f87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f47118a-6b16-5a1a-918c-cf6f9d98f21a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106783" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=4+2{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1+t)+{x}_{2}(1-t+{t}^{2}) & =4+2{t}^{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})t+{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =4+2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third  equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(2)=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+2=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d4e8e9-c4df-5b83-b927-5c59aae8c82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241547} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8e13f1-2f85-5d84-850e-77e7544ca20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241585} {:answer/id #uuid "7071d828-f406-553c-a5d6-cb2f2f212234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242181} {:answer/id #uuid "75c00306-420e-5f2d-a809-3017b554466d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242226} {:answer/id #uuid "8310d8d2-47e3-5984-9755-8b1a525681df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8310d8d2-47e3-5984-9755-8b1a525681df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242324} :answer-field/id #uuid "990c8d68-352a-5163-89c1-0134f837718f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5f3de2d-9c27-55e5-a20a-ab731f514d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-106835" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-2t+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,q(t)=2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}-2t+4)+{x}_{3}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2) & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3} \\\\ (4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+{x}_{3}{t}^{3} & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{2}-2\\cdot 1=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482978} {:answer/id #uuid "7703ce2f-e1d8-54db-a00d-63e3390949cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483022} {:answer/id #uuid "83012f55-7bea-5910-92fd-117843ef7a66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483041} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f94199-aed6-56a4-b7d3-20591c70cc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483086} {:answer/id #uuid "adc246a5-558f-5836-8eea-ace518963371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482978} :answer-field/id #uuid "215b5472-cd3f-5ffe-a96f-7f68ed482331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed08ece1-de84-563e-9900-4e9012e55ca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-106859" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2+t+{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2t-2{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1-t+{t}^{3})+{x}_{2}(1+t-{t}^{3})+{x}_{3}(2+t+{t}^{2}) & =-2t-2{t}^{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})+(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})t+{x}_{3}{t}^{2}+({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}){t}^{3} & =-2t-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the  third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+3(-2)=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(2)+2(-2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a03533aa-a487-5506-b27b-8c3bf79ec052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-5{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359149} {:answer/id #uuid "a98b954a-62d7-5f9b-85ef-f9fbfe64dd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-6{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359211} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6200a4-46ff-597b-a52b-7de1bad06ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359217} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c82c40-c70c-5c5f-a09e-18f082e57213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+4t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359299} {:answer/id #uuid "c49b3d79-b944-566f-804b-a42d9c9388d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1-3t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa6200a4-46ff-597b-a52b-7de1bad06ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359217} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b180e5f-8c33-58c8-b7dd-b3394e957bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3bc8d8b-3247-5773-8b80-0a797bc2bf9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95003" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =1\\cdot (1-t+2{t}^{2})+3\\cdot (t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-t+2{t}^{2}+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2t-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482819} {:answer/id #uuid "8a963e6d-9a8e-578a-a252-d9246861f62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=5t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483055} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfc7edd-e7f0-56c8-b0a9-ec2e8d86072c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+5t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483059} {:answer/id #uuid "90b70d6e-2507-5294-8f1f-e52a10c64626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483065} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb4aaff-4675-5ecc-b60b-c88437151648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=-6t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482819} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e2bc47-da2a-5715-9eff-8bde08f41233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "974d5dad-6c2d-5354-babc-ebd956728577" :question/math-academy-id "q-95006" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+2t+3{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-3-t-2{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =3\\cdot (1+2t+3{t}^{2})+(-1)\\cdot (-3-t-2{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =3+6t+9{t}^{2}-(-3-t-2{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =6+7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367b3a12-bda9-52ba-a70f-acf8a97b5920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358234} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3b6122-831b-5102-9fab-862057d64429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358263} {:answer/id #uuid "53b0a296-596b-53ac-85b7-9664b58cbc1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358476} {:answer/id #uuid "7a797d83-60c5-5ccc-be5e-ed2953f5f99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358815} {:answer/id #uuid "88305cdd-7847-58d7-b638-c57748efba5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367b3a12-bda9-52ba-a70f-acf8a97b5920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358234} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc375c2-091e-5e39-b3b4-55ab1a641056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c16597f8-df63-5091-b211-391b9685c9c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95016" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} & -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6\\cdot 1 & =-2 \\\\ 4{x}_{1} & =-8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3aabddb-8f21-5ac4-85e0-911c0c8d8f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359318} {:answer/id #uuid "baaa715b-7689-55ee-b14e-fd88568d265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359375} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ea90f6-c8b2-51ad-92af-372a97869184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359502} {:answer/id #uuid "e785973e-4713-55d7-92da-c991e0d3c75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359803} {:answer/id #uuid "e864d953-5e40-5d07-977c-588765dcc861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baaa715b-7689-55ee-b14e-fd88568d265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359375} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85ad7f6-b08d-59fb-bd7f-700836251219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd8162f1-9125-55c3-8d42-af30755391ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-95023" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8a372d3-d315-5749-addd-ca218934d8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366603} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab3c27f-c881-553c-99a4-41fa0ef0a58d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366604} {:answer/id #uuid "28121894-e9ce-5b0a-806b-f6ec1501699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366605} {:answer/id #uuid "78bb0746-d6c3-5d59-930f-936e9f2dd59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366606} {:answer/id #uuid "8796c8c9-b669-522b-82ea-60854c0f52be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28121894-e9ce-5b0a-806b-f6ec1501699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366605} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc10d80-64bd-56a8-a6d8-b0abd6be83f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "63b1eaca-ad47-51c0-a706-057c6e426a92" :question/math-academy-id "q-95043" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-6{t}^{3}+6t+12,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-3{t}^{2}+2t,\\,\\,q(t)=-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-6{t}^{3}+6t+12)+{x}_{2}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2)+{x}_{3}(-3{t}^{2}+2t) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18 \\\\ (-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{3}+(-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+(6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})t+(12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=19 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}-3\\cdot 2=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+(-3)=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=-3.$"}]}
